According to la xalbo {lo mlatu ka'e nenri lo botpi} means that a cat can
be inside a bottle (if e.g. that bottle is big enough) but i can't say {lo
skami ka'e djica} unless computers have emotions.

Of course, as usual it all depends on context but what {ka'e} does is that
it shows semantic relations (cat can be in a bottle, cats cannot breathe
water etc.)

However, {su'omu'ei} creates imaginary worlds.

Sorry for such a short explanation. The new version of my subjunctive
system (that is supposedly equal to the one de facto used by Nick Nicholas
at the time he was writing Lojban for Beginners) will be presented later.


